// @check
// @error member access '.length' on non-object i32[] | null
// @hint redundant type annotation: `xs` is inferred as `(i32[] | null)[]`
// REFUTATION PIN (must-error). An INDEX place is not narrowable, and this file exists so
// that the day someone makes it one they are told what else has to land with it.
//
// WHAT WAS REFUSED (inventory #2 D11). Four checker rungs make `xs[0] != null` narrow
// `xs[0]`: `placeKeyOf` keys an integer-literal index, `placeCurTy` grows an Index arm,
// `checkIndexNode` consults the overlay the way `checkMemberNode` does, and `isPathKey` —
// which decides overlay-entry vs scope-shadow, and tested only for `.` — also accepts `[`.
// Measured, they buy 72 of D11's 184 cells. They also cost 48 cells `loud check reject` ->
// `check-clean INVALID WASM`, because the EMITTER has no index-place narrowing channel at
// all (`memberPathKeyOf` is Member-shaped; the narrowed reads live in `emitMem`), and they
// break three retirement rules at once.
//
// THE THREE RETIREMENT RULES, each of which `writeRetiresNarrowing`'s own header says it
// does not need BECAUSE index places are unkeyable — "An unkeyable target (`xs[i] = …`)
// names no place and retires nothing — and no narrowing can key one either, so both sides
// stay consistent":
//
//   1. `xs[i] = null` with a VARIABLE index keys "" and retires nothing.
//   2. `xs = [null]` rebinds the ROOT, and the prefix leg matches `tgtKey + "."` only,
//      never `tgtKey + "["`.
//   3. `clr(xs)`, whose body writes `ys[0] = null`, misses because `callInvalidatesReal`
//      tests `key == ak` and `keyHasPrefix(key, ak + ".")`, and the write-effect summaries
//      record no index sub-path.
//
// Under the refused candidate all three are CHECK-CLEAN and TRAP at run time with `wasm
// trap: null reference` — the `program TRAP` column the census records as ZERO in 250,238
// cells. The three programs are kept whole in
// `scripts/silent-sweep/distilled/named/d341_sound_*.vl` with the other 48, so the standing
// 7-second gate carries the price; this file carries the REASON.
//
// This one is rule 3, the aliasing call, because it is the rule with no local spelling: the
// guarded scope never mentions the write at all.
function src(): i32[] | null { return [1, 2] }
function clr(ys: (i32[] | null)[]) { ys[0] = null }

function body() {
  const xs: (i32[] | null)[] = [src()]
  if xs[0] != null {
    clr(xs)
    print(xs[0].length)
  } else {
    print(0)
  }
}
body()
